  "reply_to_user": "Hi Hannah, thanks for reaching out. You're right: Duo was never set up on your account, and that's why the VPN keeps asking for it. The VPN needs Duo, so you won't be able to connect until setup is done. Your account and your new laptop both look fine otherwise. Setup is quick, but you need to be there with your phone, so we'll book a short session (remote or in person) with a technician. During the session we'll: 1) install the Duo Mobile app on your phone from the app store, 2) make sure Duo is installed on your laptop, 3) have you scan a QR code with your phone to link it, and 4) send you a test approval to check it works. Please reply with a few times in the next day or two that suit you (your normal hours are fine), and tell us whether you'd like remote or in person. Please have your work phone with you, charged and connected to Wi-Fi or mobile data. Until then, the VPN will keep asking for Duo, which is expected. Also, the system shows you still need to change your temporary password at your next sign-in, so please do that when prompted.",
  "internal_note": "User 12 (Hannah Lee, Finance, Payroll Specialist, not VIP), new hire. I checked her account: active, not locked, 0 failed logins, sign-in not blocked, vpn_access true. must_change_password is true and the password was set 2026-10-09, which fits a newly issued account. Duo check: enrolled false, no method or device, so Duo was never set up (KB-004 'Not enrolled'). Laptop BL-LT-0112 (Win 11) is online and checked in 2026-10-09 14:33 UTC, no warnings, 50% disk free. Sign-in logs: 9 successful sign-ins from New York (corporate and residential IPs), 0 failed_password, 0 mfa_denied, 0 hosting networks, nothing suspicious. Note: earlier VPN sign-ins (Sep 29 to Oct 7) succeeded with mfa 'none'. Duo enforcement may have been switched on recently, or those sign-ins came through a grace or bypass policy. Worth confirming. Next step: schedule a KB-004 enrollment session with the user and her phone present. Install Duo Mobile, install or verify the Duo client on BL-LT-0112, activate with the QR code, and send a test push. I've asked the user for times that work and whether she wants remote or in person. She can't use VPN until enrollment is done (noted per KB-004). No queued actions; no password reset or unlock needed.",
